From 3efbdebd7da9c833b1445f0b7d0925c2ebd7fd09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aleks <aleks.spv@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:02:40 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 143/194] ASoC: qcom: q6afe: Don't read status from HW vote
 response

The AFE_CMD_RSP_REMOTE_LPASS_CORE_HW_VOTE_REQUEST payload carries only
the client handle, it is not an aprv2_ibasic_rsp_result_t. Reading
res->status picks up whatever follows the handle, so the vote may be
reported as failed although the DSP accepted it.

Receiving the response means the vote succeeded, report status 0.

Signed-off-by: Aleks <aleks.spv@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
index 7bf936fe3..16b805cd0 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
@@ -1056,7 +1056,8 @@ static int q6afe_callback(struct apr_device *adev, const struct apr_resp_pkt *da
 		break;
 	case AFE_CMD_RSP_REMOTE_LPASS_CORE_HW_VOTE_REQUEST:
 		afe->result.opcode = hdr->opcode;
-		afe->result.status = res->status;
+		/* The payload is only the client handle, there is no status word */
+		afe->result.status = 0;
 		//printk(KERN_ERR "%s: hdr->token=%d res->opcode=%d\n", __func__, hdr->token, res->opcode);
 		if (hdr->token < Q6AFE_LPASS_CORE_HW_VOTE_MAX) {
 			afe->lpass_hw_core_client_hdl[hdr->token] = res->opcode;
